<h2 id="image-quality">Image Quality &amp; Style Control</h2>
<h3>Image Quality</h3>
<p>Canva's AI image generation delivers solid quality suitable for social media, presentations, and web graphics. The images prioritize clean, polished aesthetics over artistic experimentation. While not matching specialized tools like Midjourney in artistic quality or DALL-E 3 in creative interpretation, Canva excels at producing professional-looking graphics that integrate seamlessly into designs.</p>
<h3>Style Control</h3>
<p>Canva provides intuitive style controls optimized for non-designers:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Style Presets:</strong> Quick style options like Photo, Drawing, 3D, Pattern, and Concept Art</li>
<li><strong>Aspect Ratio Selection:</strong> Generate images in the exact dimensions needed for your design</li>
<li><strong>Template Integration:</strong> AI-generated images automatically fit into template layouts</li>
<li><strong>Brand Kit Matching:</strong> AI can generate images that complement your brand colors</li>
<li><strong>Prompt Suggestions:</strong> Built-in prompt examples and refinement suggestions</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="commercial-rights">Commercial Usage Rights</h2>
<p>Canva's commercial usage rights are straightforward and user-friendly:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Pro License:</strong> Canva Pro and Teams users get full commercial rights to AI-generated content</li>
<li><strong>Free Tier Limitations:</strong> Free users can create AI content but with restrictions on commercial use</li>
<li><strong>Content License:</strong> Generated images inherit Canva's content license terms</li>
<li><strong>Attribution Not Required:</strong> No need to credit Canva for AI-generated images</li>
<li><strong>Enterprise Clarity:</strong> Clear licensing for team and enterprise accounts</li>
<li><strong>Template Rights:</strong> Note that template usage has separate licensing from AI-generated elements</li>
</ul>
<p>For professional and commercial work, a Canva Pro subscription ensures full usage rights and access to all AI features.</p>
<h2 id="prompt-engineering">Prompt Engineering</h2>
<h3>Writing Effective Prompts</h3>
<p>Canva's AI is designed for simplicity, making it accessible even with basic prompts:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Keep It Simple:</strong> "Product photo of sneakers on white background" works well</li>
<li><strong>Specify Style:</strong> Add style keywords like "minimalist," "vibrant," or "professional"</li>
<li><strong>Think Design Context:</strong> Consider how the image will be used in your overall design</li>
<li><strong>Use Descriptive Language:</strong> "Warm sunset over ocean waves" is better than "sunset"</li>
<li><strong>Leverage Presets:</strong> Start with a style preset, then refine with your prompt</li>
</ul>
<h3>Canva-Specific Tips</h3>
<ul>
<li>Generate multiple variations and choose the best fit for your design</li>
<li>Combine AI generation with Canva's editing tools for final polish</li>
<li>Use Magic Edit to refine specific parts of generated images</li>
<li>Start with templates and add AI-generated elements strategically</li>
<li>Match generated image styles to your brand kit for consistency</li>
</ul>
